From a38525b06b35eda6b412f997395efd8c30d4335c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tommy <tommy@pham.cc>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:37:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Intro movie at high internal resolution: device-side movie
 sound, bicubic picture upscale

Sound: the movie's PCM was mixed in the mixer tick and reached the device through the 43 ms DeviceQueue that
the game thread refills once per frame, so any game-thread stall over ~40 ms (more frequent at 1440p / 4K)
left the device with silence mid-movie although seconds of the movie were queued (the WAV capture and the
"gaps" counter, which sit before that queue, never showed it). The device callback now mixes the movie from
its own copy of the PCM (ps2PushMoviePcm / ps2ClearMoviePcm fill and clear both); the producer-side copy
stays for the WAV and the played/missing accounting. TEKKEN4_AUDIO_STATS lines gain movie-missing=.

Picture: at an internal scale above 1 the movie's uploads into the target are scaled with a Catmull-Rom
bicubic pass (clamped to the 2x2 nearest texels, no halos) from the native-size staging copy instead of a
bilinear blit, redrawing the previous strip's last 2 texels with their real neighbours. Only while a movie
hands out pictures; the game's own uploads keep the filtered blit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
